DATE - show or set the date››Syntax:› DATE [/T | date]››Shows the date and asks for a new one;›RETURN keeps it. Day, day-month or›day-month-year may be typed (space›also separates). The order is›day-month-year, or month-day-year when›$DAYTIME is 1 (2 means day first).››Options:› /T  show the date only, do not ask››A date on the command line is set at›once. Needs a clock driver for correct›results.››Examples:› DATE› DATE 28-01-21› DATE /T››See also: TIME, TD, CHTD›